<!--==========Materials Progression==========


====================
MAIN MATERIALS: DURABILITY - Materials used for building, and growing building and structures.
	
	-TIER 1 MATERIALS: Materials used for general purposes.
		-Primwood: Woody. In between sandstone and limestone. most common woody. First tier of conduit trees.
		-Terramass: Organic. In between limestone and marble. Most common organic. Only grows walls and basic furnitures.
		-Terrathyst: Crystal. In between jade and gold. Very fragile to blugeoning.

	-TIER 2 MATERIALS: Materials used for advanced purposes. You need these to achieve mid-game goals.
		-Ebonmass: Organic. in between slate and granite. Upgraded variant of Terramass.
		-Elderwood: Woody. in between granite and plasteel.
		-Bioquartz: Crystal. In between gold and silver. Very fragile to bludgeoning.

	TIER 3 MATERIALS: Materials acquired from special means. End-game.
		-Deeproot: Woody. 10% weaker than Uranium. Takes a very long time and a lot of space to grow.
		-Godwood: Woody. 10% weaker than Plasteel.
		-Archwood: ???

====================
====================
ALT MATERIALS: Materials acquired outside of conventional purposes.

	-TIER 1 MATERIALS:
		-Briarwood: Woody. Only used for thin walls and defenses. Very durable and inflammable at the cost of being very cuttable.
		-Bloomwood: Woody. In between marble and slate. Second prettiest material. Not very protective.
	
	TIER 2 MATERIALS:
		-Sporewood: Woody. used for Fungal living. 25% less HP than wood, higher bludgeon and pierce resistance.

====================
====================
POTENTIAL MATERIALS: Materials that could be used for filling in spots.

	-WOODY:
		-Emberwood: Wood that absorbs sunlight and dispserses heat, which is also slowly used to grow the tree. Can be used to warm
		enclosed spaced up, but the tree needs to be properly managed in order to regulate temperature. Emberwood Trees on the
		same map share the same "network" so the more there are, the less heat each one will produce. An emberwood network can
		be used for solar weaponry, and to create bvasins that can infuse a weapon with the Soul of Summers.
		The wood itself prevents spaces from getting too cold, and can be shaped into special furniture.
	
	TIER 2 MATERIALS:
		-Sporewood: Woody. used for Fungal living. 25% less HP than wood, higher bludgeon and pierce resistance.

====================
====================
MATERIALS: PROGRESSION - in order of liklihood of aquisition.

	-EARLY-GAME MATERIALS: Materials that can pop up without focusing on them.
		-Primwood: First woody material accessible. Used for first conduit trees. Raw resource acquired through Conduit Tree.
		-Terramass: First organic material. Grown via plant, and dropped via expired Prima weaponry. Small material.
		-Soulquartz: Acquired by special Conduit Tree, by special pillar, or enemy dying to Soulbloom hediff.
		-Bloomwood: Acquired by a pawn dying to Bloompox, or by further researching Bloomwood cultivation.
		-Elderwood: Researched after completing Primwood Mastery.

	-MID-GAME MATERIALS: Materials used for advanced purposes. You need these to achieve mid-game goals.
		-Ebonmass: N/A; researched naturally.
		-Terraquartz: N/A: researched naturally.

	-SUPLEMENTARY MATERIALS: Materials that aren't strictly necessary, but have massive benefits.
		-Briarwood: Needs to be acquired by combining Prima Apex seeds + Meldsap in Elderwood Vat.
		-Sporewood: Needs to be acquired by fusing Primwood logs + Raw Fungus.
		-Linkroot: Needs to be acquired by fusing Prima Apex seeds + Raw Fungus in complete darkness.
		-Deeproot: only gifted by an allied EcoTech faction.
		-Godwood: harvested from a special event tree. Only a limited amount is harvested, but each piece can change into anything.

====================
====================
MISC MATERIALS: Materials that player minor roles.
		-Perennial Remnants: Treated as a small material.
		-Terravat Usages:
			40x Perennial Remnants + 1x Brightsap: random Perennial weapon. Refined in Terravat.
			25x Perennial Remnants + 1x Deepsap: Perennial seed. Refined in Terravat.
			Up to 100x Perennial Remnants + Up to 100x Toxsap: Up to 100x normal Terramass. Refined in Terravat.

		-Advanced usage:
			20x Perennial Remnants: Produces 10 elderwood. Refined in ???
			20x Perennial Remnants: Produces 20 terramass. Refined in ???
			20x Perennial Remnants: Produces both results. Refined in ???
		
		-Base Sap Extraction Chances:
			1% Toxsap
			1% Deepsap
			4% Brightsap
			4% Endosap
			90% No result

		-Most weapon types drop wood or fragments according to their type. These can be recycled into into Terramass, Ebonmass, or used
			to very quickly grow a product relative to the material, skipping the growth time and requirements.

====================
====================
PRIMARY UPDATE FOCUS: CRYSTALS

	The update will introduce crystals into the mod, and multiple ways to use them. They will be just as important as plants, will
	cover much of the mid-game content, and pave the way into end-game. While plants represent change and growth, crystals represent
	fortification and strength.

